# [Assign Umbrella on Rainy Days](https://leetcode.com/problems/assign-umbrella-on-rainy-days/)

## Approach: Greedy

1. Traverse the rain array and check whether it is a rainy day (`rain[i] == 1`).
2. If it is not raining, assign `"None"`.
3. If it is raining on consecutive days, assign the umbrella to the person who has used it fewer times so far.
4. If both have used it equally, assign it to Alice.
5. If it is raining but the next day is not rainy (or it is the last day), assign the umbrella to Bob.
6. Maintain separate counters for Alice and Bob to track their umbrella usage.

## Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    vector<string> assignUmbrella(vector<int>& rain) {
        vector<string>ans;
        int n = rain.size();
        int alice = 0,bob = 0;

        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            if(rain[i] == 1){
                if(i != n-1 && rain[i] == 1 && rain[i+1] == 1){
                    if(alice == bob){
                        ans.push_back("Alice");
                        alice++;
                    }
                    else if(alice > bob){
                        ans.push_back("Bob");
                        bob++;
                    }
                    else{
                        ans.push_back("Alice");
                        alice++;
                    }
                }
                else{
                    ans.push_back("Bob");
                    bob++;
                }
            }
            else ans.push_back("None");
        }
        return ans;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** \(O(N)\) — Traverse the rain array once.
- **Space Complexity:** \(O(N)\) — Store the assigned umbrella for each day.
